NAME

history - Manage command history

SYNOPSIS

    history [-c|-a|-n|-r|-w|-d N]

DESCRIPTION

Manage command history.

OPTIONS

    -c — Clear only current in-memory history.
    -d N — Delete numbered entry N from memory.
    -a — Append unsaved session commands.
    -n — Import reliably new saved entries; warn on ambiguous changes.
    -r — Import all saved entries, allowing duplicates.
    -w — Replace saved history with current memory; resolve uncertain writes.
    -h, --help — Show the built-in history help.

